cases
requirement	case	module	access program	error	reason	output	diagnostic	assertion
hooks.1	1	void-os	void-os			true		a hook event, as a harness names it, runs that hook: SubagentStart answered with its event's name
hooks.2	1	void-os	void-os			false		the input's name is the resolved pathname of the place the environment variable harness variables names holds, where it is set
hooks.3	1	void-os	void-os			true		the context is composed before the hook input is inserted, so a hook never gives back its own input
hooks.5	1	void-os	void-os		0 #<LF>	false	true	a hook input the converter rejects ends the hook as non-conforming, nothing on standard output
hooks.6	1	void-os	void-os		keeping failed<LF>	false	true	a data bank that cannot keep ends the hook as keeping failed, nothing on standard output
hooks.7	1	void-os	void-os			false		the hook input is read whole from standard input as one JSON text
hooks.8	1	void-os	void-os			true		the answer is written on standard output in UTF-8: a context holding café
